            <ArticleTitle>[Monoclonal antibodies in cardiology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>310-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Clinical efficacy of antiplatelet agents administration to reduce ischemic complications has supported the concept of atherothrombosis and plaque rupture. Specifically, administration of monoclonal antibody against platelet membrane receptor glycoprotein IIb/IIa was shown to be highly effective whenever percutaneous intervention is performed in the setting of unstable coronary syndrome. The in-hospital use of glycoprotein IIb/IIIa is unanimously recommended in these situations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
